Verse 1:
[C]I sing the mighty power of God, [G]That [Am]made the moun[G]tains[C] rise,
[C]That spread the flowing seas abroad, [G]And [Am]built the loft[G]y [C]skies
[C]I [G7]sing the wisdom [C]that ordained The [G7]sun to rule the da[C]y;
[G]The [C]moon shines full at [F]His com[Am]mand [F]And [C]all the stars [G7]o[C]bey.

Verse 2:
[C]I [G]sing [Am]the goodness [G]of [C]the Lord,
[C]who [G]filled [Am]the [G]earth [C]with food,
[C]who [G7]formed [C]the creatures [G7]thru [C]the Word,
[G][C]and [F][Am]then [F]pronounced [C][G7]them [C]good.
[C]Lord, [G]how [Am]thy [G]wonders [C]are displayed,
[C]where'er [G]I [Am]turn [G]my [C]eye,
[C]if [G7]I [C]survey the [G7]ground [C]I tread,
[G][C]or [F][Am]gaze [F]upon [C][G7]the [C]sky!

Verse 3:
[C]There's [G]not [Am]a plant [G]or [C]flower below,
[C]but [G]makes [Am]thy [G]glories [C]known,
[C]and [G7]clouds [C]arise, [G7]and [C]tempests blow,
[G][C]by [F][Am]order [F]from [C][G7]thy [C]thrown;
[C]while [G]all [Am]that borrows [G]life [C]from thee
[C]is [G]ever [Am]in [G]thy [C]care;
[C]and [G7]everywhere [C]that [G7]we [C]can be,
